A1. What your wife is to you. ~ ON
A3. What they throw out of ships. ~ ANCHORS
A6. The first sound a reader of JUDGE makes at opening the magazine. ~ HA
A8. What a bedtime story does to you. ~ LULL
A9. Even the best laid ones gang agley. ~ PLAN
A10. What most actors think they are. ~ IT
A11. What Uncle Sam does to himself in regard to Europe. ~ ISOLATE
A16. The seventh note in music. ~ SI
A17. One hundred per centers. ~ AMERICANS
A19. It says the same thing you do. ~ ECHO
A21. How most men give money to their wives. ~ DOLE
A23. What she says when you try to kiss her. ~ NO
A24. A pronoun in the objective case. ~ ME
A25. What you say when boarding a vessel. ~ AHOY
A26. What a girl likes to have in her stocking. ~ ROLL
A28. Abbreviation for number. ~ NO
A29. What the little tough boy says for verbs. ~ VOIBS
A32. An exclamation. ~ LO
A33. Water does it. ~ DRIP
A36. United States of America backwards. ~ ASU
A37. That's that. ~ THAT
A39. What you see on every cent. ~ TRUST
A41. How you say mister in India. ~ SAHIB
A43. A college boy in a raccoon coat. ~ SIMP
A45. They're called but few are chosen. ~ MANY
A47. Twenty million people chew it. ~ SPEARMINT
A49. What the college boy says at the football game. ~ RAH
A50. There's nothing new under it. ~ SUN

D1. You used to see one in a cockail. ~ OLIVE
D2. What you think of a man who doesn't agree with you. ~ NUT
D3. It's the man who pays it. ~ ALIMONY
D4. Why her sweetie went away. ~ HALITOSIS
D5. What every girl likes. ~ SPENDER
D6. Third person singular present tense of a verb (laugh that off). ~ HAS
D7. An Egyptian plant. ~ ANISE
D12. Southeast. ~ SE
D13. A conjunction. ~ OR
D14. An athletic club. ~ AC
D15. What she says when she says good-by. ~ TA
D17. What the detective says when he finds a clue. ~ AH
D18. A parting word used with long. ~ SO
D20. A body of Roman soldiers. ~ COHORTS
D22. What your mother used to sing to you. ~ LULLABY
D25. Another conjunction. ~ AND
D27. He had a wife that got too fresh. ~ LOT
D30. Every young man sows one. ~ OAT
D31. You see a lot of them on Fifth avenue. ~ BUS
D34. They love to fight. ~ IRISH
D35. Where Volstead would like all of us to spend all of our time. ~ PUMP
D37. A particle (conjunction). ~ THAN
D38. What you give to unpopular guests. ~ HINTS
D40. An automobile went down the road at fifty miles an hour. ~ SPED
D42. In between. ~ AMID
D44. Not a seat in the theater. ~ SRO
D46. His son had the same name as his. ~ JR
D48. After a hard night most people are all —. ~ IN


